			"Message": "feat(Wind): Add IPC Channel registry TypeScript module\n\nAdd Source/IPC/Channel.ts as a TypeScript mirror of the Rust Channel enum in Element/Common/Source/IPC/Channel.rs. This file provides the authoritative wire string constants for all IPC communication between Wind and Mountain.\n\nThe module exports a default object with all channel names mapped to their wire string format (e.g., \"commands:execute\", \"file:read\"). TypeScript consumers can import and use these channels for type-safe IPC invocations via IPCService.invoke(), ensuring compile-time validation against typos at the call site.\n\nThe file is hand-kept in lockstep with the Rust Channel enum — both must agree on the number and wire strings for correct dispatch.",
			"SHA": "2164b922070af98d8eac43a46f6c960412dc7b57"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-21T18:32:07Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1037,
				12
			],
			"Message": "feat(Wind): Load product.json at build time for configuration\n\nImplement Atom I5: refactor ResolveConfiguration to fetch product identity from /product.json (generated by Maintain/Script/ResolveProductConfig.sh from .env.Land variables) instead of hardcoded strings.\n\n- Add LoadProductJson() async function that fetches /product.json with fallback to minimal defaults\n- Update product configuration fields (nameShort, nameLong, applicationName, version, commit, urlProtocol, dataFolderName, serverApplicationName) to use resolved values\n- Preserve backward compatibility: network failures fall through to base defaults allowing degraded boot with version mismatch warning\n\nThis enables single-source-of-truth product identity without hardcoded version strings in the codebase. The Target/ build outputs are regenerated to reflect the new configuration resolution.",
			"SHA": "cc360e37a2ae2757410b42cc94580bff1eccd8d4"
		},
